{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation in Go, matching the Hyperledger Fabric primary language and the GoDoc documentation requirement.",
    "Reuse the existing Fabric proto-generated Go types (common.Config, common.ConfigUpdate, msp.FabricMSPConfig, msp.MSPConfig) rather than introducing new types.",
    "Build as an idiomatic Go library package following existing Fabric configtx conventions (function-based API that returns updated config plus a computed ConfigUpdate envelope).",
    "Use the Go standard library crypto/x509 for the minimal certificate validation required by U4 (KeyUsageCertSign, BasicConstraintsValid/IsCA).",
    "Library returns the ConfigUpdate envelope (and the resulting Config block) ready to be plugged into the standard Fabric signature collection workflow; signing is out of scope.",
    "Idiomatic examples are written in examples_test.go files so they appear in GoDoc and are verified by `go test`.",
    "Helpers for reading (U7, U8) navigate the standard config tree (Application→orgs→AnchorPeers / Orderer) and return strongly typed structs rather than raw protos.",
    "Mutators (U1, U2, U3, U4) are implemented as pure functions of an existing Config block to keep them composable and testable.",
    "For U3, revoked certificates are added to the FabricMSPConfig.revocation_list (serial numbers as raw bytes), consistent with how Fabric already consumes that field."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced Go developer who is already familiar with the Hyperledger Fabric v1.4 codebase and its configtx building blocks.",
    "Existing Fabric proto definitions, configtx utilities, and proto-generated Go types are available and do not need to be regenerated.",
    "A test network and CI are already in place; only test code for the new functions is added.",
    "Signing, ordering, and broadcast are explicitly out of scope — the library produces the ConfigUpdate envelope and stops there, matching the acceptance criteria.",
    "Certificate validation in U4 is 'minimal' as stated: only KeyUsageCertSign and the CA basic-constraints attribute are checked (no chain verification, no expiry checks beyond what the standard library surfaces when parsing).",
    "Examples in U5 and U6 are single-file, self-contained GoDoc examples that compile and run as `Example...` tests.",
    "No major architectural redesign of the existing config package is required — the work is additive.",
    "The anchor peer list in U1/U2 is modified for one organization at a time, identified by the org's MSP ID.",
    "Orderer configuration retrieved in U8 is the full orderer group config (consenter, batcher, organization, addresses, policies) so callers can re-use it as a base for updates."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Design and analysis of existing Fabric configtx code",
      "activity_description": "Read the spec, review the existing Fabric configtx/configtxlator code, study the AnchorPeers, Orderer, and FabricMSPConfig proto structures, and design the package API, file layout, and function signatures for all eight user stories."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement U1: add anchor peer to channel config",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes an existing Config block/transaction and an anchor peer (host:port) for a given org MSP ID, adds it to the org's AnchorPeers list, and returns the updated Config plus a ConfigUpdate envelope ready for the signature workflow."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement U2: remove anchor peer from channel config",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes an existing Config block/transaction and an anchor peer to remove for a given org MSP ID, removes it from the AnchorPeers list, and returns the updated Config plus a ConfigUpdate envelope."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement U3: revoke a certificate in FabricMSPConfig",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes an existing Config block/transaction and a certificate issued by the target MSP, appends the certificate's serial number to the FabricMSPConfig.revocation_list field, and returns the updated Config plus a ConfigUpdate envelope."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement U4: add root CA certificate to MSP with validation",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes an existing Config block/transaction, an MSP ID, and a PEM-encoded CA certificate. The certificate is parsed with crypto/x509 and rejected if it is missing KeyUsageCertSign or the CA basic-constraints attribute. On success, the certificate is added to the MSP's CA certs list and the updated Config plus a ConfigUpdate envelope are returned."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement U7: helper to retrieve existing anchor peers",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes a Config block/transaction and an org MSP ID and returns that org's current anchor peers without requiring the caller to manually walk the config tree."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement U8: helper to retrieve existing orderer configuration",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes a Config block/transaction and returns a config.Orderer value (consensus type, batcher settings, addresses, organizations, policies) that the caller can mutate and pass back to a corresponding UpdateOrdererConfiguration function."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Write GoDoc example for updating channel transactions (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Author an idiomatic example in examples_test.go that creates a config update with multiple changes (e.g. anchor peer and orderer batch size), computes the ConfigUpdate envelope, and signs it. Must be runnable by `go test` and visible in the package's GoDoc."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Write GoDoc example for creating channel transactions (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Author an idiomatic example in examples_test.go that builds a new channel creation transaction and signs it. Must be runnable by `go test` and visible in the package's GoDoc."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Unit tests for all new functions",
      "activity_description": "Write table-driven unit tests covering happy paths and failure modes (missing org, duplicate anchor peer, certificate missing KeyUsageCertSign, certificate not a CA, etc.) for A2 through A7."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Update integration/example tests for U7 and U8 helpers",
      "activity_description": "Extend the existing example/integration tests in the config package so they demonstrate usage of the new anchor peer and orderer config retrieval helpers, as called out in the acceptance criteria of U7 and U8."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Code review, bug fixing, and final polish",
      "activity_description": "Address code-review feedback, fix bugs surfaced by unit and example tests, tighten error messages, ensure GoDoc comments are complete on every exported symbol, and verify the package builds cleanly with go vet, golint, and the project's CI pipeline."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 94
  }
}
```

